And if you went back to that planning piece,

00:13:01.214 --> 00:13:02.455
what do you see in that?

00:13:02.795 --> 00:13:04.336
Dinner has always been water,

00:13:05.097 --> 00:13:05.417
pan,

00:13:05.577 --> 00:13:05.857
pot,

00:13:05.957 --> 00:13:06.197
you know,

00:13:06.277 --> 00:13:08.578
like on the stove eight minutes and then like you're done.

00:13:08.919 --> 00:13:13.401
That makes me want to look at what meals have been like throughout life.

00:13:13.621 --> 00:13:16.443
I never remember ever eating family dinners like at the table.

00:13:16.951 --> 00:13:19.452
And I would always eat mac and cheese.

00:13:19.833 --> 00:13:21.073
All the adults said was just like,

00:13:21.074 --> 00:13:21.153
oh,

00:13:21.154 --> 00:13:22.474
it's just in his picky eater phase.

00:13:22.475 --> 00:13:23.174
Yeah.

00:13:23.214 --> 00:13:24.315
Anytime I try something new,

00:13:24.935 --> 00:13:26.236
even if I like the first bite of it,

00:13:26.636 --> 00:13:29.758
I almost will always have an involuntary just gag.

00:13:29.858 --> 00:13:31.879
What's the experience that goes with that gagging?

00:13:32.159 --> 00:13:32.840
What have you noticed?

00:13:32.880 --> 00:13:33.140
Oh,

00:13:33.141 --> 00:13:33.740
it's embarrassing.

00:13:34.181 --> 00:13:34.381
Like,

00:13:34.382 --> 00:13:35.401
it's super embarrassing.

00:13:35.541 --> 00:13:37.162
I think through the lens of trauma a lot.

00:13:37.742 --> 00:13:39.443
So have you experienced physical abuse?

00:13:39.483 --> 00:13:39.644
Yes.

00:13:39.884 --> 00:13:41.004
And so if you think of fight,

00:13:41.104 --> 00:13:41.404
flight,

00:13:41.445 --> 00:13:42.145
or freeze.

00:13:42.485 --> 00:13:42.625
Yeah,

00:13:42.626 --> 00:13:43.205
I was a freezer.

00:13:43.426 --> 00:13:45.747
Can you relate those feelings now to what it's like?

00:13:45.967 --> 00:13:46.727
approaching foods?

00:13:47.187 --> 00:13:50.768
If I sit down and like I'm in a room with the intention of trying a new food,

00:13:50.848 --> 00:13:56.910
then my stress like immediately skyrockets like and it like stays up until like the penultimate moment hits where like

00:13:57.590 --> 00:13:59.431
I try it and then like I have that gag reflex.

00:13:59.451 --> 00:13:59.731
I'm like,

00:13:59.732 --> 00:13:59.931
all right,

00:13:59.932 --> 00:14:00.271
out of the way.

00:14:00.311 --> 00:14:00.791
I didn't like it.

00:14:00.851 --> 00:14:05.213
And then like it's done and then like it goes down or like I get out of the room and then it goes down.

00:14:05.273 --> 00:14:07.753
You basically draw the stress curve with your hand whenever you're talking.

00:14:07.754 --> 00:14:07.873
Yeah,

00:14:07.874 --> 00:14:08.233
I know.

00:14:09.754 --> 00:14:11.074
You're aware of what's happening.

00:14:11.194 --> 00:14:13.515
That's part of what My job is to teach people.

00:14:14.055 --> 00:14:16.877
to understand what's happening and that it will have a beginning and end.

00:14:16.937 --> 00:14:19.558
It's going to come up and it's going to go down like a wave.

00:14:20.459 --> 00:14:24.561
But we often feel it rising and think that it's going to continue to just go up.

00:14:25.001 --> 00:14:29.944
What we want to do as we're approaching foods is know what might happen.

00:14:30.684 --> 00:14:31.445
And regardless,

00:14:31.565 --> 00:14:35.227
we're going to be working on building skills to keep you grounded in your body.

00:14:35.387 --> 00:14:39.089
We'll be looking at a hierarchy of foods that you'll establish.

00:14:39.389 --> 00:14:39.549
Right.

00:14:40.029 --> 00:14:43.071
And so it's exposure and then it...

00:14:43.231 --> 00:14:44.752
it starts to extinguish some of the fear.

00:14:45.232 --> 00:14:46.192
We build a new pathway,

00:14:46.392 --> 00:14:52.115
and that pathway looks like I actually can feel this feeling and go forward and live.

00:14:52.215 --> 00:14:59.018
I just hope I can get to a place where I'm equipped to deal with what I'm feeling when I try new foods.

00:14:59.058 --> 00:15:01.159
That way I can try new foods at a neutral,

00:15:01.519 --> 00:15:06.841
unbiased look instead of just having the massive anxiety associated with it.

00:15:07.221 --> 00:15:10.483
It's completely separated from who I am.

00:15:11.023 --> 00:15:13.608
It's like a relic of whenever I was in a worse mental place.

00:15:13.969 --> 00:15:15.211
And it just kind of stuck with me.

00:15:15.612 --> 00:15:17.877
That is a really great way to conceptualize it.

00:15:18.157 --> 00:15:18.818
It's a part of you.

00:15:19.455 --> 00:15:20.376
You don't need any more.

00:15:20.696 --> 00:15:20.816
Yeah.

00:15:20.976 --> 00:15:24.118
But that is so deeply ingrained that it's still there.

00:15:24.518 --> 00:15:24.638
Yeah.

00:15:24.939 --> 00:15:25.819
You have a lot of insight.

00:15:25.979 --> 00:15:27.140
You're pretty motivated to do it.

00:15:27.340 --> 00:15:27.480
Yeah.

00:15:27.620 --> 00:15:27.740
Oh,

00:15:27.741 --> 00:15:27.840
yeah,

00:15:27.880 --> 00:15:28.221
for sure.

00:15:28.501 --> 00:15:31.983
So I can like slowly open up like what restaurants I go to and stuff.

00:15:32.023 --> 00:15:33.344
You want to be able to go to more restaurants.

00:15:33.444 --> 00:15:34.104
More restaurants.

00:15:34.124 --> 00:15:36.426
Just be more social with eating and stuff,

00:15:36.446 --> 00:15:36.666
you know.

00:15:37.046 --> 00:15:43.190
What we'll do from here is just look at frequency and when you can come in next so that we can make the most of your time and your commute.

00:15:43.410 --> 00:15:44.311
I'm super excited.

00:15:44.531 --> 00:15:44.831
All right,

00:15:44.951 --> 00:15:45.232
Austin,

00:15:45.292 --> 00:15:46.393
thank you so much for coming in.

00:15:46.553 --> 00:15:46.813
Yes,

00:15:46.913 --> 00:15:48.014
I'm so excited to work with you.

00:15:48.134 --> 00:15:48.935
Safe travels back.

00:15:48.975 --> 00:15:49.835
Thank you very much.

00:15:49.895 --> 00:15:50.536
You have a good day.

