It was wonderful meeting Austin.

00:15:54.299 --> 00:16:01.265
He has so much insight and such an openness to developing a better understanding.

00:16:01.525 --> 00:16:04.928
He's truly motivated to do this work,

00:16:05.068 --> 00:16:07.430
even though he knows it's going to be really uncomfortable for him.

00:16:07.550 --> 00:16:08.831
I think it went better than expected,

00:16:09.051 --> 00:16:09.351
actually.

00:16:09.632 --> 00:16:10.412
She's definitely really cool.

00:16:10.413 --> 00:16:11.453
It definitely gives me hope,

00:16:11.853 --> 00:16:13.335
especially since she's so confident.

00:16:13.395 --> 00:16:13.615
you

00:16:14.083 --> 00:16:16.084
How much I'll succeed like makes me,

00:16:16.264 --> 00:16:17.104
makes me feel really good,

00:16:17.224 --> 00:16:18.225
makes me feel really confident.

00:16:18.765 --> 00:16:20.986
Mac and cheese for many is a comfort food.

00:16:21.266 --> 00:16:21.866
For Austin,

00:16:22.046 --> 00:16:25.488
while it has had that effect,

00:16:25.928 --> 00:16:27.328
it's not about that anymore.

00:16:28.149 --> 00:16:30.630
He would like to be able to eat other foods,

00:16:30.710 --> 00:16:31.730
to have variety,

00:16:32.070 --> 00:16:33.471
and to eat vegetables.

00:16:34.271 --> 00:16:37.133
But he feels crippled and paralyzed by the idea of doing so.

00:16:37.833 --> 00:16:42.215
And so he falls back on mac and cheese because it's what his brain and body will allow.

00:16:43.135 --> 00:16:45.577
where he can have some peace.

00:16:46.258 --> 00:16:51.763
And so you're having to work against your body to get yourself to sit with food in your mouth.

00:16:52.443 --> 00:16:56.887
The perceived threat is so much more than the actual experience.

00:16:57.488 --> 00:17:01.932
But you can't convince your body of that without doing a lot of work to chip away at it.

00:17:05.535 --> 00:17:06.956
I'm not ashamed of who I am.

00:17:07.657 --> 00:17:10.079
I wouldn't want my kids to see me just eating mac and cheese all the time.

00:17:11.039 --> 00:17:13.321
While my kids eat a more balanced meal than me,

00:17:13.501 --> 00:17:14.201
oh my god.

00:17:15.182 --> 00:17:19.145
I found out about selective eating disorder just by pure luck.

00:17:19.445 --> 00:17:24.348
It was just like a nameless thing that just hung over me and like I just thought like that was just one of my idiosyncrasies,

00:17:24.368 --> 00:17:25.529
like one of my little quirks.

00:17:26.970 --> 00:17:29.292
I definitely didn't choose to be like this at all.

00:17:30.452 --> 00:17:34.255
This selective eating disorder has its hooks in me and it's just like holding me back.

00:17:34.815 --> 00:17:36.276
It's exciting thinking like

00:17:36.937 --> 00:17:40.059
I could get to a point where like I'm able to try new foods and possibly

00:17:40.691 --> 00:17:40.951
you know,

00:17:41.092 --> 00:17:42.053
like them and enjoy them.

00:17:50.526 --> 00:17:50.847
Dang it,

